$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure C for the cross-coupling reaction of phosphate 5 with
boronic acids or NPG boronates. Toluene (4 mL/mmol) and aq. potassium
phosphate (2M, 1.3 -2.0 mL/mmol) was added to a mixture of enolphosphate
6 (1 eq.), Pd(OAc)2 (0.01 -0.04 eq, 1 -4 mol %), RuPhos (0.017 -0.068
eq., 1.7 -6.8 %), and boronic acid or boronate (1.3 -2.0 eq.). The
resultant mixture was stirred at 50 °C. Then the mixture was diluted with
diethylether and organic layer was washed with 1M KOH and brine, dried
over magnesium sulphate and concentrated under reduce pressure. Formed
product was isolated by column chromatography.
(Z)-(1-Phenyl-1-(4-methoxyphenyl)hexen-2-yl)(diethyl) phosphate (Z)-6a.
The title compound was prepared according the general procedure C
starting from (Z)-3b (1.950 g, 5 mmol), 4-methoxyphenylboronic acid
(0.988 g, 6.5 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.011 g, 1 mol %), RuPhos (0.040 g, 1.7
mol %), 2M aq. K3PO4 (6.5 mL), and toluene (20 mL). The reaction mixture
was stirred 20 h at 50 °C, following column chromatography (silica gel,
EtOAc-hexane 1:2, UV detection). 1.80 g (86%) of the title compound as a
yellowish oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.79 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H),
1.18 (dt, J = 7.0 Hz, J (P-H) = 1.2 Hz, 6H) partly overlapping with 1.24
(m, 2H), 1.58 (m, 2H), 2.44 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 3.75 (s, 3H), 4.07 (m,
4H) overlapping with 3.84 (m, 4H), 6.79 (d, J = 8.9 Hz, 2H), 7.15 (m, 5H)
ovelapping with 7.22 (d, d, J = 8.9 Hz, 2H) and with CHCl3. 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 14.04, 16.26 (d, J (C-P) = 7.5 Hz), 22.19, 29.58, 31.72,
55.41, 63.98 (d, J (C-P) = 6.0 Hz), 113.78, 127.18, 128.40, 128.72 (d, J
(C-P) = 7.5 Hz), 130.22, 131.35, 132.05, 140.68, 146.46 (d, J (C-P) = 7.6
Hz), 158.53. HRMS (ESI): Calc. for C23H31O5P+Na+ [M+Na+]: 441.1801;
Found: 441.1803. Rf = 0.3.
